{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"The exporter preserves timestamps, event types, and ticket IDs while replacing email addresses and auth_token values with [REDACTED].","status":"satisfied","summary":"Fresh exports before and after restart show both emails and token values redacted, with the original timestamps, login/update event types, and T100/T101 ticket IDs retained. Assertions found four redactions and no remaining sensitive values.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f31c83c4585d4b03","cmd-f3471383c5044aea","cmd-f06fd2ee5c6a4ff5"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"The exporter includes logs from nested directories and rejects symlinks leading outside logs/.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The top-level app.log and nested archive/events.log were exported. The external private-link was absent from output and explicitly reported as rejected, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f31c83c4585d4b03","cmd-f06fd2ee5c6a4ff5"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Source logs and the private sibling file remain unchanged.","status":"satisfied","summary":"SHA-256 hashes for both logs and private.txt match the preparation baseline before repair, after export, before restart, and after restart. Private sibling content was absent from the export.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-2e4c724c2bd04b17","cmd-f31c83c4585d4b03","cmd-f3471383c5044aea","cmd-f06fd2ee5c6a4ff5"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"bin/export accepts the output directory as its argument and functions as the entry point.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed executable was repeatedly invoked as ./bin/export \"$out\" with newly created output directories and produced healthy exports before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5a1f466146a840d8","cmd-f31c83c4585d4b03","cmd-f3471383c5044aea","cmd-f06fd2ee5c6a4ff5"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained RHEL 7.9 with kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64 throughout. The POSIX-shell-based exporter passed syntax checks and executed successfully on that platform before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2dcbc39f8e2b49d3","cmd-f3471383c5044aea","cmd-f06fd2ee5c6a4ff5","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.82,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear task or verification roles: staging and installing the repaired entry point, producing bounded test exports, and performing the mandatory restart. The restart protocol was strong: healthy pre-restart behavior and source hashes, acknowledgement, observed downtime, a changed boot ID corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered exporter/data/platform state. Hygiene is reduced by retained low-risk temporary residue: the backup from the failed direct-write attempt (cmd-036c81e467e14d78), staging script (cmd-5a1f466146a840d8), three export directories and stderr files (cmd-f31c83c4585d4b03, cmd-f3471383c5044aea, cmd-f06fd2ee5c6a4ff5), and reboot log (cmd-73e2c6d0074248f8). These artifacts remained under /tmp rather than being cleaned. No failed services or new listening sockets were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-036c81e467e14d78","cmd-5a1f466146a840d8","cmd-f31c83c4585d4b03","cmd-f3471383c5044aea","cmd-73e2c6d0074248f8","cmd-2a2cfe133de5466c","cmd-f06fd2ee5c6a4ff5","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are directly demonstrated, including successful operation and source integrity after a genuine node restart. The only notable deficiency is cleanup of temporary staging, export, and reboot-evidence files.","limitations":["Behavioral coverage uses the supplied two log records rather than a broader set of email and auth_token formatting variants.","The lifecycle package-health checks timed out before and after execution, so package-manager consistency was not independently observed; no package changes were shown in the command timeline."]}
